  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 159 AM CDT Wed Jul 29 2026\n\nToday a longwave trof aloft sets up over the northeast CONUS keeping \nus in northwest flow aloft as the upper ridge begins to shift west. \nBehind the front today we have temperatures back into the mid to \nupper 80s. Dewpoints will be lower today, in the mid 60s, and the \nsfc high pressure keeps us dry and mainly clear (though there may be \nsome upper level smoke present). Tomorrow is more of the same while \nan upper level trof approaches from the northwest and crests over \nthe ridge. \n\nThis upper trof begins to descend toward the CWA from the northwest \non Friday pushing a sfc low just ahead of it. Rain chances come\nback on Friday morning in the west and push eastward, peaking \nin the evening and overnight at around 70-80% in the NBM. Rain \nchances then continue to pop up each afternoon through the \nmiddle of next week.",
